From: dyxushuai <dyxushuai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reject sparse or cross-OUI FE MAC upper ranges

The FE can only encode one 3-byte prefix and one continuous [lmin,lmax]
interval per LAN/WAN role. Preferring a dual-WAN macvlan upper set that
uses a different OUI from the physical WAN address, or that spans far
more addresses than the real unicast count, programs a huge PPE match
window and demotes the physical MAC to software receive.

Only program the WAN FE range from upper unicast when:
  1) upper shares the physical OUI (or there is no physical yet), and
  2) the continuous span is dense enough (small holes allowed).

Otherwise keep the physical FE range and leave mismatched/sparse upper
addresses on the software receive path. This preserves IPv4 macvlan FOE
offload prepare/unwrap while refusing unsafe FE table updates.

Signed-off-by: dyxushuai <dyxushuai@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -297,26 +297,49 @@
 	}
 
 	if (upper.valid && !upper_conflict) {
-		selected = upper;
-
-		/* Preserve acceleration for matching physical addresses. */
-		for (i = 0; i < n_phys; i++) {
-			if (memcmp(selected.prefix, phys_addrs[i],
-				   sizeof(selected.prefix)))
-				continue;
-			airoha_mac_range_include(&selected, phys_addrs[i]);
-		}
-
-		/* FE holds one global 3-byte prefix per role. Prefer upper so
-		 * macvlan/session MACs hit PPE; make demotion of a
-		 * different-OUI physical address observable.
+		bool same_oui = !physical.valid ||
+				!memcmp(physical.prefix, upper.prefix,
+					sizeof(physical.prefix));
+		u32 span;
+
+		/*
+		 * FE encodes one prefix + one continuous [lmin,lmax]. Prefer
+		 * upper only when safe: same OUI as physical (when present)
+		 * and dense enough that the interval is not a multi-million
+		 * PPE match window for unrelated addresses.
 		 */
-		if (physical.valid &&
-		    memcmp(physical.prefix, selected.prefix,
-			   sizeof(physical.prefix)))
+		if (!same_oui) {
 			dev_warn_ratelimited(eth->dev,
-					     "%s upper unicast OUI differs from physical; physical addresses leave the hardware MAC range and use software receive\n",
+					     "%s upper unicast OUI differs from physical; keep physical FE range, upper uses software receive\n",
 					     role);
+			selected = physical;
+		} else {
+			selected = upper;
+
+			/* Preserve acceleration for matching physical addresses. */
+			for (i = 0; i < n_phys; i++) {
+				if (memcmp(selected.prefix, phys_addrs[i],
+					   sizeof(selected.prefix)))
+					continue;
+				airoha_mac_range_include(&selected,
+								 phys_addrs[i]);
+			}
+
+			span = selected.lmax - selected.lmin + 1;
+			/*
+			 * Allow small holes (e.g. 3 addrs spanning 4) but
+			 * reject pathological dual-WAN pools.
+			 */
+			if (span > selected.count &&
+			    (span > selected.count * 8 ||
+			     span > selected.count + 64)) {
+				dev_warn_ratelimited(eth->dev,
+						     "%s upper MAC range is sparse (%u entries span %u addresses); keep physical FE range, upper uses software receive\n",
+						     role, selected.count,
+						     span);
+				selected = physical;
+			}
+		}
 	} else {
 		selected = physical;
 	}
@@ -328,11 +351,6 @@
 		dev_warn_ratelimited(eth->dev,
 				     "%s upper unicast MAC prefixes differ; upper traffic will use software receive fallback\n",
 				     role);
-	if (selected.lmax - selected.lmin + 1 > selected.count)
-		dev_warn_ratelimited(eth->dev,
-				     "%s MAC match range is sparse (%u entries span %u addresses); unrelated addresses may reach PPE lookup\n",
-				     role, selected.count,
-				     selected.lmax - selected.lmin + 1);
 
 	if (eth->fe_mac_prog[lan].valid &&
 	    !memcmp(eth->fe_mac_prog[lan].prefix, selected.prefix,

